<title>BELGIUM: EU vets Philips/Hewlett-Packard deal.</title>
<headline>EU vets Philips/Hewlett-Packard deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it had opened a routine probe into plans by Philips Lighting BV and Hewlett-Packard Europe BV to take joint control of a lighting components company, JV BV.</p>
<p>Philips, a unit of Philips Electronics NV, manufactures and sells illumination products. Hewlett-Packard Europe is a holding company for all non-U.S. activities of Hewlett-Packard Co.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement it would investigate whether the joint venture violated European Union rules banning mergers that create or strengthen a dominant position.</p>
<p>It has one month to clear the deal or open an in-depth investigation.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
